  "_comment": "Recipe catalog (real data drives the schema). Each recipe is an option the player can pick from the alchemy / brew UI. The record names what it is, lists the reagents required (keys are Item ids, values are integer counts), and names the Item id produced on a successful brew (`result_item`). Today every recipe's `result_item` happens to equal its own `id` \u2014 that's a convenience of the seed data, not a contract; future recipes can produce an arbitrary Item. DC, result count, and other crafting mechanics are intentionally deferred and will land on Recipe (or an adjacent model) when the brew-execution path is implemented. See docs/data_dictionary/recipe.md.",
